    <bpmn:process id="W_W1930" name="W1930. Consignment Physical Inventory &amp; Vendor Reconciliation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly consignment reconciliation; annual physical inventory
Frequency: Monthly reconciliation; annual wall-to-wall count
Volume: ~1,500–2,000 consignment SKUs × 200 stores
Owner: AP Manager
Participants: AP Manager, Store Manager, Vendor, External Auditor
Source: workflow W1930 — Consignment Physical Inventory &amp; Vendor Reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1930_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1930_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1930_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1930_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1930_Lane2" name="AP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1930_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1930_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1930_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1930_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1930_Start5" name="Monthly consignment reconciliation; annual physical inventory">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1930_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1930_Task6" name="Monthly: system generates consignment stock reconciliation report per vendor…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly: system generates consignment stock reconciliation report per vendor: (a) opening balance (units), (b) additions (receipts), (c) reductions (sales), (d) returns to vendor, (e) adjustments (damages, shrinkage), (f) closing balance (units), (g) compare system closing balance to vendor&#x27;s recorded balance
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): AP Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1930_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1930_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1930_Task7" name="AP Manager investigates discrepancies: (a) system shows more than vendor…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AP Manager investigates discrepancies: (a) system shows more than vendor: possible unrecorded receipt or vendor counting error, (b) system shows less than vendor: possible unrecorded sale, theft, damage not reported, (c) resolve discrepancies within 5 business days, (d) adjust consignment stock in system with documented reason
Responsible (R): AP Manager
Accountable (A): Accounting Manager
Duration: 1–2 days/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1930_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1930_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1930_Task8" name="Annual physical inventory: (a) consignment stock counted alongside owned…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Annual physical inventory: (a) consignment stock counted alongside owned inventory during wall-to-wall count per W42, (b) consignment stock tagged separately in count sheets, (c) vendor invited to observe count of their consignment stock, (d) count results shared with vendor within 10 business days, (e) discrepancies resolved per consignment agreement terms
Responsible (R): Store Manager / AP Manager
Accountable (A): Accounting Manager
Duration: Per annual count</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1930_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1930_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1930_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1930_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1930_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-174 (ensure consignment &amp; VMI settlement integrity.) | - operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: AP Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
