    <bpmn:process id="W_W1932" name="W1932. Consignment Price Change &amp; Promotional Price Handling" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor price change; BuildRight promotional event
Frequency: ~20–30 consignment price changes/month
Volume: ~1,500–2,000 consignment SKUs
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Pricing Analyst, VP Merchandising, Vendor
Source: workflow W1932 — Consignment Price Change &amp; Promotional Price Handling</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1932_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1932_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1932_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1932_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1932_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1932_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1932_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1932_Start3" name="Vendor price change; BuildRight promotional event">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1932_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1932_Task4" name="Vendor-initiated price change: (a) vendor notifies Category Manager of…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Vendor-initiated price change: (a) vendor notifies Category Manager of consignment cost change (up or down), (b) Category Manager evaluates impact: (i) if cost increase: can BuildRight maintain current SRP and margin?, (ii) if cost decrease: should SRP be reduced or maintain to capture additional margin?, (c) update consignment cost in system (impacts COGS at next sale), (d) if SRP changes: initiate price change per W40
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30 min/change</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1932_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1932_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1932_Task5" name="BuildRight promotional event on consignment items: (a) Category Manager…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: BuildRight promotional event on consignment items: (a) Category Manager negotiates promotional consignment cost with vendor (vendor funds a portion of the discount), (b) system applies promotional SRP at POS (standard promo mechanics per W13), (c) system calculates: (i) promotional revenue, (ii) promotional consignment cost, (iii) margin during promo period, (iv) vendor contribution to discount
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per promo event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1932_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1932_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1932_Task6" name="Post-promotion: (a) system reverts to standard consignment cost and SRP, (b)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Post-promotion: (a) system reverts to standard consignment cost and SRP, (b) Category Manager reviews promo performance: sell-through lift, vendor contribution, net margin
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 day/post-promo</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1932_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1932_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1932_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1932_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1932_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-376 (ensure controlled execution — Consignment Inventory Operations (PA-45.1).) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
